    "situation": "The bank system has recovered. The recovery check ran five looks, and the last two in a row at 60 s were clean.",
    "background": "About 12 s before diagnosis, an operator changed payments max_transfer_minor from 1000000 to 1. Around the same time, a reconciliation session held a write lock on the ledger, clearing exited (exit code 15, last 11 s ago), and the primary screening service slowed to p95 1821 ms against a 15 ms baseline.",
    "assessment": "There were four root causes, and the incident commander fixed each one itself. It reverted payments max_transfer_minor to 1000000, ended the reconciliation session holding the ledger lock, and restarted clearing, which has not exited since. It also failed screening over to screening-standby, because primary timeouts above payments' 1.0 s limit were failing 100% of screening calls.",
    "recommendation": "Ask the operator why max_transfer_minor was set to 1, and find out why clearing exited. Repair the primary screening service before failing back from screening-standby. Have the operations team review transfers rejected for the limit, ledger writes blocked by the lock, the interrupted reconciliation batch, and payments that failed screening, and confirm none were lost or need to be retried."
  },
